course: dictionary
lesson: 11980
title: Ceramic: a word for baked clay
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ceramic is a hard material made by shaping clay and baking it at a very high heat in a kiln. You can work out its meaning from the words around it. «The shop sold ceramic mugs and plates.» Mugs and plates are things we use at the table, so ceramic tells us what they are made of.
explain: Ceramic can also be a noun. «Ceramics is her favourite art lesson.» Here ceramics means the craft of making pots and other things from clay. «She made a small ceramic bowl in class.» Here a ceramic is the object itself.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «She made a small clay bowl» still makes sense, so ceramic means made of baked clay. Ceramic is hard, but «He dropped the ceramic cup and it cracked» shows it can break if it falls.
fact: Ceramic means a hard material made by shaping clay and baking it at a very high heat.
fact: Ceramics means the art or craft of making pots and other things from clay.
fact: A ceramic is an object made of this material, such as a mug, plate or tile.
fact: Ceramics are hard and strong, but they are brittle, so they can break if dropped.
fact: Baking clay in a kiln is a change that cannot be reversed: a baked pot cannot turn back into soft clay.
exercise: «The shop sold ceramic mugs and plates.» What is the word ceramic telling us? | How many people bought them | The price of the mugs | The colour of the shop | *What the mugs and plates are made of
exercise: «Ceramics is her favourite art lesson, and she makes pots from clay.» What does ceramics mean here? | A school subject about the sky | A kind of dance | *The art or craft of making things from clay | A type of cold weather
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that names a hard material baked from clay: «The bathroom had white tiles and a ceramic sink.» | bathroom | *ceramic | white | sink
test: «He dropped the ceramic bowl and it shattered on the floor.» Why did the bowl break? | It was too cold in the room | Ceramic is always soft and bends easily | *Ceramic is brittle and can break when it is dropped | The bowl was made of wood
test: Which sentence uses ceramics to mean objects, not the craft? | «Ceramic is a hard material used for tiles.» | *«The shelf held three ceramics, all painted by hand.» | «Ceramics is her favourite lesson at school.»
exam: Which sentence is the best definition of ceramic? | Ceramic is a type of metal that melts easily | Ceramic is a soft, wet clay that is never baked | Ceramic is the sound a plate makes when it is washed | *Ceramic is a hard material made by shaping clay and baking it at a very high heat
